{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they did not listen to Moses.</b> They did not accept words of comfort." "<b>Shortness of spirit.</b> Anyone who is in distress — his spirit and breath are short, and he cannot draw out his breath. Close to this matter I heard in this passage from Rabbi Baruch bar Rabbi Eliezer, and he brought me proof from this verse: ״בַּפַּעַם הַזֹּאת אוֹדִיעֵם אֶת יָדִי וְאֶת גְּבוּרָתִי וְיָדְעוּ כִּי שְׁמִי ה׳״ (Jeremiah 16) — we learn that when the Holy One, blessed be He, fulfills His words, even for punishment, He makes known that His name is YHWH, and all the more so fulfillment for good. And our Sages interpreted it for a different matter: that Moses said, ״Why have You done evil״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״חֲבַל עַל דְּאָבְדִין וְלָא מִשְׁתַּכְּחִין״ — I have reason to complain about the loss of the patriarchs; many times I revealed Myself to them as El Shaddai and they did not say to Me, ״What is Your name?״, and you said, ״What is His name?״ — what shall I say to them?" "<b>And also I established, etc.</b> And when Abraham sought to bury Sarah he found no grave until he purchased for much money, and so with Isaac — they disputed with him over the wells he dug, and so Jacob — ״וַיִּקֶן אֶת חֶלְקַת הַשָּׂדֶה״, to pitch his tent, and they did not question My ways, and you said, ״Why have You done evil?״ But the midrash does not settle with the verse for several reasons: first, that ״and My name is YHWH — they did not ask Me״ was not said; and if you say He did not inform them that such is His name — behold, at the outset, when He revealed Himself to Abraham between the pieces, it says ״אֲנִי ה׳ אֲשֶׁר הוֹצֵאתִיךָ מֵאוּר כַּשְׂדִים״ (Genesis 15); and furthermore, how does the juxtaposition continue in the words that he juxtaposes here — <b>And also I have heard, etc. Therefore say to the children of Israel</b>? Therefore I say: let the verse be settled according to its plain sense, each utterance in its own place, and the interpretation will be interpreted as it says ״הֲלוֹא כֹה דְבָרִי כָּאֵשׁ נְאֻם ה׳ וּכְפַטִּישׁ יְפוֹצֵץ סָלַע״ (Jeremiah 23) — it splits into many sparks (Sanhedrin 34)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:51.383641594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}